 ### Cosign and Rekor
 
-To verify Cosign signed artifacts, use `rekor-cli` or `curl` to [pull the entry from Rekor](https://edu.chainguard.dev/open-source/sigstore/rekor/how-to-verify-file-signatures-with-rekor-or-curl/).
+OpenBao release artifacts are signed with [Cosign](https://docs.sigstore.dev/cosign/overview/)
+and the signatures are recorded in the public [Rekor](https://docs.sigstore.dev/logging/overview/)
+transparency log. The recommended way to verify them is with the `cosign verify-blob`
+command, which checks the signature against the certificate embedded in the
+signature bundle and confirms that the signing event is present in the
+transparency log.
 
-For example, to verify `checksums.txt` with the `checksums.txt.sig` stored locally:
+First, download the release artifact, its signature, and its certificate:
 
 ```shell-session
-$ SHASUM="$(openssl sha256 -r checksums.txt | awk '{print $1}')"
-bc53476e7e69c98650bf69690caf1aa32dc08c19735375819ae3b29bb9c2b733
-$ curl -X POST -H "Content-type: application/json" 'https://rekor.sigstore.dev/api/v1/index/retrieve' --data-raw "{\"hash\":\"sha256:$SHASUM\"}"
-24296fb24b8ad77aedcc1a0cea8b33a04926d6f3b8db35107a1e864c007bb4aa84416a5153cc0bca
-$ UUID=24296fb24b8ad77aedcc1a0cea8b33a04926d6f3b8db35107a1e864c007bb4aa84416a5153cc0bca
-$ curl -X GET "https://rekor.sigstore.dev/api/v1/log/entries/${UUID}" > response.json
-$ jq -r ".[\"$UUID\"].body" < response.json | base64 -d | jq -r '.spec.signature.publicKey.content' | base64 -d > certificate.pem
-$ base64 -d < checksums-freebsd.txt.sig > checksums-freebsd.txt.rawsig
-$ openssl pkeyutl -verify -certin -inkey certificate.pem -sigfile checksums-freebsd.txt.rawsig -in checksums-freebsd.txt -rawin
-Signature Verified Successfully
+$ OS="freebsd"
+$ ARCH="x86_64"
+$ PLATFORM="$OS_$ARCH"
+$ VERSION=$(curl -s https://api.github.com/repos/openbao/openbao/releases | jq -r '.[0] .tag_name' | cut -d'v' -f2-)
+$ RELEASE="bao_$VERSION_$PLATFORM.tar.gz"
+$ wget https://github.com/openbao/openbao/releases/download/v$VERSION/$RELEASE
+$ wget https://github.com/openbao/openbao/releases/download/v$VERSION/$RELEASE.sig
+$ wget https://github.com/openbao/openbao/releases/download/v$VERSION/$RELEASE.pem
+```
+
+Then verify the artifact with `cosign verify-blob`. The `--certificate-identity`
+and `--certificate-oidc-issuer` flags pin the verification to the OpenBao
+release workflow, and `--rekor-url` points at the public transparency log:
+
+```shell-session
+$ cosign verify-blob \
+    --certificate "$RELEASE.pem" \
+    --signature "$RELEASE.sig" \
+    --certificate-identity-regexp '^https://github.com/openbao/openbao/.github/workflows/release.*$' \
+    --certificate-oidc-issuer https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com \
+    --rekor-url https://rekor.sigstore.dev \
+    "$RELEASE"
+Verified OK
 ```
+
+If you have a signature bundle (`.sigstore` or `.bundle` file) instead of
+separate signature and certificate files, pass it with `--bundle`:
+
+```shell-session
+$ cosign verify-blob \
+    --bundle "$RELEASE.sigstore" \
+    --certificate-identity-regexp '^https://github.com/openbao/openbao/.github/workflows/release.*$' \
+    --certificate-oidc-issuer https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com \
+    --rekor-url https://rekor.sigstore.dev \
+    "$RELEASE"
+Verified OK
+```
+
+:::note
+
+Older releases may only provide a detached `.sig` file without a certificate.
+For those, you can still inspect the entry in the Rekor transparency log using
+`rekor-cli` or `curl`, as described in the
+[Rekor documentation](https://docs.sigstore.dev/logging/overview/).
+
+:::
